PE 853: Pisano Periods 1 / Pisano周期1

=== Pisano Period Definition ===
π(m) = smallest k > 0 such that F_k ≡ 0 (mod m)
                            and F_{k+1} ≡ 1 (mod m)
where F_0 = 0, F_1 = 1.

=== Small Values ===
m    π(m)    m    π(m)    m    π(m)
------------------------------------------------
 1       1   11      10   21      16
 2       3   12      24   22      30
 3       8   13      28   23      48
 4       6   14      48   24      24
 5      20   15      40   25     100
 6      24   16      24   26      84
 7      16   17      36   27      72
 8      12   18      24   28      48
 9      24   19      18   29      14
10      60   20      60   30     120

=== Prime Pisano Periods ===
p    π(p)    p mod 5    p-1    2(p+1)   Formula
------------------------------------------------------------
  2       3        2          1       6     π(p)|2(p+1)
  3       8        3          2       8     π(p)|2(p+1)
  5      20        0          4      12     π(5)=20
  7      16        2          6      16     π(p)|2(p+1)
 11      10        1         10      24     π(p)|p-1
 13      28        3         12      28     π(p)|2(p+1)
 17      36        2         16      36     π(p)|2(p+1)
 19      18        4         18      40     π(p)|p-1
 23      48        3         22      48     π(p)|2(p+1)
 29      14        4         28      60     π(p)|p-1
 31      30        1         30      64     π(p)|p-1
 37      76        2         36      76     π(p)|2(p+1)

=== Prime Power Patterns ===
p=2 (π=3): π(2)=3 π(4)=6 π(8)=12 π(16)=24
p=3 (π=8): π(3)=8 π(9)=24 π(27)=72 π(81)=216
p=5 (π=20): π(5)=20 π(25)=100 π(125)=500 π(625)=2500
p=7 (π=16): π(7)=16 π(49)=112 π(343)=784 π(2401)=5488

=== Multiplicativity ===
π(2·7=14) = 48, lcm(π(2),π(7)) = 48 → ✓
π(2·11=22) = 30, lcm(π(2),π(11)) = 30 → ✓
π(3·7=21) = 16, lcm(π(3),π(7)) = 16 → ✓
π(3·11=33) = 40, lcm(π(3),π(11)) = 40 → ✓
π(5·7=35) = 80, lcm(π(5),π(7)) = 80 → ✓
π(5·11=55) = 20, lcm(π(5),π(11)) = 20 → ✓

=== Cumulative Sum ===
Σ_{m=1}^{50} π(m) = 2352

=== PE Answer ===
44511058204
